# Hub UI — patch, do not rebuild

`tools/sandbox_control/templates/index.html` is the whole hub chrome. Do **not** replace it (or `app.js` tab lists) with a “simpler” layout.

## Do
- Smallest possible edit: insert or change only the feature asked for.
- Keep existing top tabs, Admin subtabs, Demos cards (Buzz Scout, Docs portal), header links, Calendar, Clients, script tags, and `?v=` bumps for files you actually touch.
- If a tab’s JS/Python still exists on disk, the HTML must still load it.

## Don’t
- Reconstruct `index.html` or `app.js` from memory of an older hub.
- Remove My Calendar, Buzz Scout, Docs, or other working hub UI unless Brian explicitly asks to remove that thing.
- Drop `/api/demos` fields (`scout`, `docs`) or unhook `hub_calendar.register` as a side effect of another change.
- Restart the hub unless a Python file you changed requires it.

My Emails stays off unless he asks to bring it back.
